.Dd March 12, 2026
.Dt DEVICE_RESET 9
.Os Substrate
.Sh NAME
.Nm device_reset
.Nd reset a device subtree through driver callbacks
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In kern/device.h
.Ft int
.Fn device_reset "struct device *dev"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn device_reset
function walks a device subtree, invokes each bound driver's
.Va reset
callback, and restores the recorded device power state to
.Dv PM_STATE_D0
on success.
.Pp
Children are reset before their parent so subordinate state is quiesced before
the parent transport or bridge is reinitialized.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The
.Fn device_reset
function returns 0 on success, the first non-zero error returned by a driver
callback, or
.Dv -EINVAL
if
.Fa dev
is
.Dv NULL .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr device 9 ,
.Xr driver 9
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Fn device_reset
interface first appeared in Substrate.
